	(text "\"The VTBIAS capacitor should be a good quality electrolytic.\nFor very high clock frequencies it is recommended to connect\na smaller value capacitor (e.g., 100nF ceramic X7R) in\nparallel to reduce impedance of the bypass capacitance.\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.636 0.636)
			)
		)
		(uuid "05c31285-7ffc-4dbf-ae6e-ac9ff186868f")
	)
	(text "\"An unbroken ground plane directly beneath the SSI2100 and its associated clock and signal traces is the single most effective measure. Avoid\nsplits or cutouts in the ground plane under any high-frequency trace, as these force return currents to detour, enlarging the current loop and\nradiating accordingly. The return current for the clock signal will naturally flow in the ground plane directly below the clock trace, provided the\nplane is continuous; interrupting this path is a common source of otherwise-mysterious clock bleed.\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.68 41.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.636 0.636)
			)
		)
		(uuid "104391f1-3a97-4651-a218-2a3968ca1902")
	)
	(text "\"Route the clock trace as a direct, short path between the clock source and\nthe SSI2100, avoiding long parallel runs alongside input or output signal traces. Where a clock trace must cross an audio trace, route them on\ndifferent layers and cross at right angles to minimize capacitive coupling. Guard traces (grounded copper running either side of the clock line)\ncan further contain the field, though they are only effective when tied to a solid ground plane at frequent intervals such as 5mm or less.\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 151.13 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.636 0.636)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1594cfc9-1275-4c41-9292-5ed81d237c2a")
	)
	(text "TODO: could add additional stage for higher frequency cutoff"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 231.14 100.33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1a28bcbd-041a-46bc-8c82-359adf98ffb8")
	)
	(text "\"Under certain signal conditions a considerable\nshort pulse of current can occur at the start\nof the sampling period. It is recommended that\nan external 1nF capacitor and series 100Ω\nresistor are used to isolate op amp outputs\nfrom this dynamic load, which could otherwise\ncause the op amp to ring at each sample point.\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 148.59 77.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2012539f-faba-41ca-8c3c-1438ec52cd3b")
	)
	(text "ceramic decoupling cap very close\nalso needs good 10u+ supply filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 267.97 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
